<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 02-JAN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 02-JAN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Phil, near 17s/109e, is moving west at 10 mph. It has top winds of 40 mph and will continue to weaken while dissipating during the next 24-36 hours. The threat to shipping will decrease.  </p>
<p>Flooding, mudslides, sinkholes, and other storm-related problems continue in the US Northwest. More rainfall is expected into Friday as problems continue.  </p>
<p>THERE ARE NO FURTHER EMERGENCY WEATHER STATEMENTS</p>
</text>
